Meson identifies emcc as compiler id 'emscripten', not 'clang', so glib's
probe for which unsigned type size_t is a typedef of was skipped and gsize
fell back to the first type of the same width ('unsigned int'). Emscripten's
size_t is 'unsigned long' (both 32 bits on wasm32), so passing a gsize* where
a size_t* is expected fails with -Werror=incompatible-pointer-types (e.g.
glib/gconvert.c). Run the probe for emcc too; it is clang underneath.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1786,7 +1786,7 @@
 # Do separate checks for gcc/clang (and ignore other compilers for now), since
 # we need to explicitly pass -Werror to the compilers.
 # FIXME: https://github.com/mesonbuild/meson/issues/5399
-if cc.get_id() == 'gcc' or cc.get_id() == 'clang'
+if cc.get_id() == 'gcc' or cc.get_id() == 'clang' or cc.get_id() == 'emscripten'
   foreach type_name, size_compatibility : g_sizet_compatibility
     g_sizet_compatibility += { type_name: size_compatibility and
       cc.compiles(
